  q(MW,'Which MMWR series publishes detailed CDC guidelines, such as treatment recommendations for sexually transmitted infections?','Recommendations and Reports',['QuickStats','Notes from the Field','The weekly notifiable disease tables'],'A','MMWR also publishes Surveillance Summaries, which give in-depth analyses of surveillance data.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'In a picnic outbreak, 36 of the 40 ill guests ate potato salad. Why is this percentage useful?','A suspect food should explain most cases',['It is the attack rate among eaters','It is the odds ratio','It proves the salad caused the outbreak'],'B','A strong suspect should be eaten by most cases, but it still needs to be compared with non-eaters.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Guests ate at noon, and five became ill at 4, 5, 6, 8 and 10 p.m. What is the median incubation period?','6 hours',['5 hours','6.6 hours','10 hours, based on the last case'],'C','The incubation periods are 4, 5, 6, 8 and 10 hours, and the middle value is 6.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Since 2016, large U.S. hepatitis A outbreaks have mainly affected which groups?','People who use drugs and people experiencing homelessness',['Infants under 6 months','Dairy farmers','Travelers returning from cruises in the Caribbean'],'D','Poor access to sanitation and close contact helped spread the virus person to person.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'The 2019 outbreak of e-cigarette or vaping product use–associated lung injury (EVALI) was strongly linked to which substance?','Vitamin E acetate',['Nicotine salts','Propylene glycol only','Menthol flavoring added to nicotine'],'A','Vitamin E acetate was found in lung fluid samples from most patients tested.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Most U.S. measles outbreaks begin when which event occurs?','An unvaccinated traveler brings the virus from abroad',['The vaccine stops working in adults','Mosquitoes carry the virus','The virus spreads through tap water'],'B','These are called importations, and outbreaks then spread in communities with low vaccine coverage.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Congenital syphilis cases have risen sharply in the U.S. What is the main way to prevent them?','Testing and treating pregnant people in time',['Vaccinating newborns','Giving antibiotics to all infants','Avoiding breastfeeding for the first six months of life'],'C','Many cases occur when testing is missed or treatment is not given at least 30 days before delivery.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'A rare, nearly always fatal brain infection follows swimming in warm freshwater when water goes up the nose. Which organism causes it?','Naegleria fowleri',['Giardia','Cryptosporidium','Legionella, spread through inhaled mist'],'D','Drinking contaminated water does not cause infection; the ameba must enter through the nose.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Alpha-gal syndrome, an allergy to red meat, is mainly linked to bites from which tick?','The lone star tick',['The blacklegged (deer) tick','The brown dog tick','The soft tick found in rodent nests'],'A','Alpha-gal reactions often appear hours after eating red meat, which makes them hard to recognize.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Why does the CDC call carbapenem-resistant Enterobacterales (CRE) “nightmare bacteria”?','They resist even last-resort antibiotics',['They are spread by mosquitoes','They cause only mild illness','They can be cured with any common antibiotic'],'B','CRE can also pass resistance genes to other bacteria, so facilities use strict infection control.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'On an epi curve for a point-source outbreak, one case occurs well after all the others. What might it represent?','A secondary case or a separate exposure',['Proof of a vector','A data entry error only','The index case of the outbreak'],'C','Outliers can give clues, such as person-to-person spread or a late exposure to the same source.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'A clinician suspects foodborne botulism. When should the health department be notified?','Immediately, by phone',['Within one month','At the end of the year','Only after lab confirmation weeks later'],'D','Rapid reporting lets officials release antitoxin and find the contaminated food before others eat it.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Which CDC system collects data on healthcare-associated infections such as CLABSI from hospitals?','The National Healthcare Safety Network (NHSN)',['BRFSS','FoodNet','The Youth Risk Behavior Surveillance System'],'A','NHSN data help hospitals compare their infection rates with national benchmarks.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Which CDC system compiles U.S. birth and death certificate data?','The National Vital Statistics System (NVSS)',['VAERS','ILINet','PulseNet'],'B','NVSS data are used to track causes of death, life expectancy and birth trends.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'What is the leading cause of death from injury among U.S. children aged 1 to 4 years?','Drowning',['Poisoning','Falls','Burns from house fires'],'C','Most of these drownings happen in home swimming pools, so fencing and supervision matter.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Acute flaccid myelitis (AFM), which causes sudden limb weakness, has peaked in late summer and is linked to which virus?','Enterovirus D68',['Measles virus','Hepatitis B virus','Rotavirus'],'D','AFM mostly affects children and has shown a pattern of rises every two years in the past.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Which drug does the CDC recommend for suspected Rocky Mountain spotted fever in patients of all ages, including young children?','Doxycycline',['Amoxicillin','Azithromycin','Ciprofloxacin'],'A','Treatment should start right away because delays raise the risk of death.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Many recent Salmonella outbreaks have been linked to contact with which animals?','Backyard poultry such as chicks and ducklings',['Pet cats','Horses','Dogs adopted from shelters'],'B','People should wash their hands after handling birds and should not kiss or snuggle them.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Why can a chronic carrier of Salmonella Typhi cause outbreaks for years?','Bacteria persist in the gallbladder and are shed in stool',['The bacteria live in the lungs','Carriers always have high fevers','The bacteria spread only through mosquito bites'],'C','“Typhoid Mary” infected many people while working as a cook in the early 1900s.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Outbreaks of E. coli infection have been linked to eating raw cookie dough. Which ingredient was the source?','Raw flour',['Chocolate chips','Sugar','Vanilla extract added after mixing'],'D','Flour is a raw agricultural product and is not treated to kill germs.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'A study reports a risk ratio of 0.5 for an exposure. What does this suggest?','The exposure is linked to lower risk',['The exposure doubles risk','There is no association','The study must contain an error'],'A','A risk ratio below 1.0 suggests a protective effect, such as from a vaccine.',MMWR),
  q(MW,'Influenza vaccine effectiveness is often estimated by comparing vaccination among patients with flu-like illness who test positive and those who test negative. What is this design called?','A test-negative design',['A cross-sectional survey','A randomized trial','An ecological study of countries'],'B','The test-negative design is a type of case-control study that reduces differences in care-seeking.',MMWR)
